# OnePick Tools

OnePick Tools is a Docker-deployed media toolbox. Current focus: a compact media parsing workbench that handles one or many shared links, applies output presets, proxies single-file downloads, and archives multi-item or batch results into ZIP files.

## Deploy

```bash
cd /opt/docker/onepick
docker compose up -d --build --force-recreate
```

Default exposed port:

```text
http://<dev-host>:3877
```

## Pages

- `/` — main parser UI
- `/config` — runtime status, parser status, Cookie status, recent history

## APIs

- `GET /api/health`
- `GET /api/runtime`
- `GET /api/self-test`
- `GET /api/tools`
- `GET /api/history?limit=50`
- `DELETE /api/history`
- `POST /api/inspect`
- `POST /api/parse` — accepts `input` plus optional `preferences` such as `{ "mode": "video", "quality": "1080" }` or `{ "mode": "audio" }`
- `POST /api/shortcut/download` — iOS Shortcuts friendly single-file endpoint. Accepts `input`, `mode`, `quality`, and optional `itemIndex`; parses the link and streams the best-quality downloadable item directly. It does not ZIP multi-item results. If there are multiple candidates and the best item is over 100MB, it returns HTTP 409 with a candidate list so Shortcuts can ask which one to download.
- `GET /api/download?url=...&filename=...`
- `POST /api/archive`

### iOS Shortcuts

Use `Get Contents of URL` with method `POST`, request body `JSON`, and URL:

```text
http://192.168.199.8:3877/api/shortcut/download
```

Example body:

```json
{
  "input": "Shortcut Input",
  "mode": "video",
  "quality": "1080"
}
```

For audio-only:

```json
{
  "input": "Shortcut Input",
  "mode": "audio",
  "quality": "best"
}
```

If a parser returns multiple media items, this endpoint picks the best-quality downloadable item. If that best item is over 100MB, the response is JSON:

```json
{
  "needsSelection": true,
  "candidates": [
    { "index": 0, "filename": "video.mp4", "quality": "1080p", "filesizeMB": 128 }
  ]
}
```

After the user chooses one, call the same endpoint again with `itemIndex` set to the selected candidate's `index`.

## Cookies

Put Netscape-format cookies here when a platform requires login/captcha bypass:

```text
cookies/douyin.txt
cookies/xiaohongshu.txt
cookies/kuaishou.txt
cookies/youtube.txt
cookies/instagram.txt
cookies/twitter.txt
cookies/facebook.txt
```

The directory is mounted read-only into the container at `/app/cookies`.

## Data

Runtime history is persisted in:

```text
data/history.jsonl
```

It is trimmed by `HISTORY_MAX_LINES` in `docker-compose.yml`.

## Self test

From the host:

```bash
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:3877/api/self-test | python3 -m json.tool
```

From inside the container/project:

```bash
ONEPICK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000 npm run self-test
```

From host against published port:

```bash
ONEPICK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3877 docker compose exec onepick-tools npm run self-test
```

## Current dedicated parsers

- Douyin
- Xiaohongshu
- Kuaishou
- Bilibili
- YouTube
- Weibo
- TikTok

Generic fallback uses `yt-dlp`. Recognized generic platforms include Instagram, X/Twitter, Facebook, Vimeo, Reddit, Dailymotion, SoundCloud, Pinterest, Threads, Tumblr, and Twitch.
